    "reflection": "Effortlessly neutralizing opposition taunts through instantaneous double entendre and good-natured comedic delivery.",
    "content": "In 1969, following the demise of Arignar Anna, Kalaignar M. Karunanidhi assumed the office of Chief Minister of Tamil Nadu.\n\nThe Leader of the Opposition was Congress stalwart P. G. Karuthiruman, a seasoned orator with an incisive wit.\n\nDuring a debate on policy consistency, Karuthiruman decided to taunt the young Chief Minister with past rhetoric:\n\"Mr. Chief Minister! In your early years, your party raised an emotional slogan across every platform: 'Either we attain Dravida Nadu, or we go to the graveyard!'\nNow, having abandoned the separate state demand, you are comfortably seated on the treasury benches. Where is that graveyard you promised? Are you currently residing in the graveyard?\"\n\nCongress benches broke into gleeful laughter.\n\nKarunanidhi rose smoothly from his seat, a playful smile curling his lips:\n\"Mr. Speaker! My esteemed friend Karuthiruman has inquired about our whereabouts with great concern, asking if we are in the graveyard.\nI shall give him a very simple and direct answer:\nNo, friend Karuthiruman! We are certainly not in the graveyard; we are right here, sitting comfortably alongside you in the Tamil Nadu Legislative Assembly!\"\n\nThe assembly chamber exploded into roaring laughter!\n\nThe double entendre was brilliant: while Karunanidhi meant they were physically present in parliament, the implication that sitting with the opposition was equivalent to the graveyard left Karuthiruman himself grinning in admiration.\n\nBy refusing to get angry and meeting sarcasm with sparkling wit, Karunanidhi kept assembly debates lively, memorable, and cultured.",
